  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Git View",
      "text": "Review, stage, commit and push the session repository's git changes from the\nHarness conversation view.\n\n[中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "A **Git** tab in the conversation view ring, after Trajectory. It reads the\nrepository the session is working in — no path to configure, no second UI."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- **Every project in the workspace** — the repositories around the working\n  directory, each with its own branch, markers and commit. They are committed\n  separately, never across repositories. Projects with nothing pending fold into\n  one row so the ones you are actually working on stay on screen.\n- **Change groups** — conflicts, staged, unstaged and untracked, each with\n  folder rows that fold a whole subtree and stage or discard it in one action.\n- **Three ways to read a file** — whole file with the changes marked, changes\n  only as a unified diff, or side by side. Remembered across sessions.\n- **Edit and save** — open a working-tree file in the panel and write it back,\n  guarded by the version the read returned.\n- **Branches, stash, pull, sync** — and a fetch, refresh and discard group.\n- **Commit and push** — an AI-written commit message from the staged diff, a\n  commit button that commits, and a push button that lists every commit it would\n  publish before it publishes them."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Untracked directories stay folded until opened, and opening one asks git about\nthat directory alone. A working tree with twenty thousand untracked files costs\nthe same to list as one with twenty.\n\nA repository nested inside another one is not offered as a folder in its\nparent's file list, because git will not describe what is inside it to the\nparent and opening one would show nothing. It is one of the projects instead."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires dsh 0.2.0-rc.2 or newer, Node 22.19+ or 24+, and a session whose\nworking directory is a git repository.\n\nIt is in the plugin market. To install it by hand, either path works:\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "prebuilt, no build-approval step",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile <profile> add https://github.com/shinchen6/dsh-git-view/releases/latest/download/dsh-git-view.tgz"
    },
    {
      "section": "or build from source",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile <profile> add shinchen6/dsh-git-view\n```\n\nThen restart the profile and open the **Git** tab in a conversation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Screenshots",
      "text": "The push button lists what it would publish first.\n\nThe commit box enlarges from its top-right control."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[Apache-2.0](LICENSE)"
    }
